COMPANY EMPLOYEE POLICY

1. Annual Leave Policy

Employees are entitled to 20 days of annual leave per calendar year.
Employees must submit leave requests through the employee portal.
Leave requests should normally be submitted at least 3 working days before the requested leave date.
Emergency leave may be requested without the normal advance notice.

2. Work From Home Policy

Eligible employees may work from home up to 2 days per week.
Work from home requires manager approval.
Employees working remotely must remain available during normal working hours.
Employees must maintain a stable internet connection while working remotely.

3. Working Hours

The standard working hours are 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM, Monday to Friday.
Employees receive a one-hour lunch break.
Employees are expected to be available during their scheduled working hours.

4. Notice Period

The standard notice period for full-time employees is 30 days.
Employees who wish to resign must submit a formal resignation request to their manager and HR.
The notice period begins from the date the resignation is formally accepted.

5. Remote Work Security

Employees must use company-approved devices when accessing confidential company information remotely.
Employees must not share company credentials with other individuals.
Confidential company documents must not be stored on personal cloud storage services.

6. Employee Support

Employees can contact the Human Resources department for questions regarding leave, attendance, benefits, and workplace policies.
Technical issues should be reported to the IT support team.
